    fix(useFileDrop, lib.rs, tauri.conf): switch to Tauri native drag-drop for honest path provenance (P0 Foxtrot)
    
    Why:
    Codex's P0-Echo re-review BLOCKED the bookmark-provenance fix because
    the production path was non-functional: OrganizerLayer never passed a
    finderClient to useFileDrop, and even if it had, the HTML5 hook only
    delivers `File.name` basenames which the Rust `validate_user_path`
    gate deterministically rejects (not absolute). The end-to-end contract
    "every authorized path has user provenance" was therefore false.
    
    What:
    Phase-1 spike (docs/workflow/roadmap/codex-reviews/p0-foxtrot-native-dnd/SPIKE-FINDINGS.md)
    established that the originally-anticipated changes to tauri.conf.json,
    lib.rs, and window.rs were NOT required: `grid_*` windows already use
    Tauri native DnD by default, and OrganizerGridContent.tsx already
    consumes absolute paths off `tauri://drag-drop`. The transparent
    click-through `main` window CANNOT receive native DnD anyway (AppKit
    setIgnoresMouseEvents_(YES) routes drag sessions through). The minimum
    honest fix is therefore to add bookmark registration to the existing
    absolute-path flow, not to refactor DnD configuration.
    
    Phase-2 implementation (this commit):
    
    - OrganizerGridContent.tsx now accepts an optional `finderClient` prop
      and calls `client.registerBookmark(path)` for every absolute path
      from `tauri://drag-drop` BEFORE emitting ORGANIZER_FILE_DROP_EVENT
      cross-window. Fire-and-forget per path; failures logged but do NOT
      abort the drop UX.
    
    - apps/desktop/src/windows/GridWindow.tsx constructs a FinderClient
      via `createFinderClient(useTauriInvoke().invoke)` and passes it
      into OrganizerGridContent. The Grid window is the only surface
      that receives absolute paths from Tauri DnD, so it is the only
      honest registration point.
    
    - OrganizerLayer.tsx adds defensive bookmark registration on the
      main-window receiver of ORGANIZER_FILE_DROP_EVENT. Idempotent on the
      Rust side; quick-filters non-absolute paths before the IPC call.
    
    - useFileDrop.ts is now documented as visual-only on the click-through
      `main` window (HTML5 drag indicator). The deprecated `finderClient`
      prop is accepted but ignored (with a JSDoc redirect to
      OrganizerGridContent). Stopped calling `registerBookmark` with
      basenames — that path was a deterministic no-op that masqueraded as
      provenance.
    
    - bookmarks.rs: `register_path_bookmark<R: Runtime>` and
      `clear_path_bookmark<R: Runtime>` are now generic over Tauri runtime
      so the SAME `#[tauri::command]` body runs in production (Wry) and in
      the new MockRuntime integration tests. New `ipc_integration_tests`
      module drives the commands through `tauri::test::get_ipc_response` —
      the actual invoke-handler dispatcher with JSON serialization —
      addressing Codex's P1 "test sidesteps the public IPC" finding.
    
    - finder.rs: `ensure_path_authorized_test_helper` (`#[cfg(test)]`,
      `pub(crate)`) exposes the gate `reveal_in_finder` / `open_path`
      consult, so the integration tests can assert admission without
      spawning `open -R`.
    
    - Cargo.toml: `[dev-dependencies] tauri = { features = ["test"] }` so
      `MockRuntime` is available to cargo tests only.
    
    Scope:
    - apps/desktop/package.json: + `@repo/core` workspace dep
    - apps/desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml: + dev-dependency `tauri["test"]`
    - apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/commands/bookmarks.rs: generic <R>; new ipc_integration_tests
    - apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/commands/finder.rs: pub(crate) test helper
    - apps/desktop/src/windows/GridWindow.tsx: construct + pass FinderClient
    - packages/plugin-organizer/src/OrganizerGridContent.tsx: optional finderClient prop + register-on-drop
    - packages/plugin-organizer/src/OrganizerLayer.tsx: defensive registration on cross-window receiver
    - packages/plugin-organizer/src/hooks/useFileDrop.ts: visual-only; stop basename registration
    - packages/plugin-organizer/src/hooks/useFileDrop.test.ts: new regression tests
    - docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md: §4 drop-event mechanism paragraph
    - docs/workflow/roadmap/codex-reviews/p0-foxtrot-native-dnd/SPIKE-FINDINGS.md: new
    - docs/workflow/roadmap/codex-reviews/g3-organizer-batch/PROCESS-NOTE.md: P0-Foxtrot resolution
    - packages/grid-shell-organizer-content/docs/dev_log.md: Work Log row
    
    NOT touched: tauri.conf.json, lib.rs, window.rs (spike found the
    originally-anticipated DnD-config refactor was unnecessary — the
    current architecture already routes drops through `grid_*` windows
    correctly).
    
    Risk:
    - G1.2 SHIPPED invariants (grid-shell-organizer-content boundary):
      public surface `OrganizerGridContent` unchanged in name/shape (added
      one optional prop); event names, payload shapes, emit targets,
      drag-drop lifecycle byte-identical; Host-vs-Organizer boundary
      unchanged. SHIPPED is reaffirmed.
    - G1.4 (scoped-grid-events): no event-channel changes; ORGANIZER_FILE_DROP_EVENT
      payload shape and gridId scoping preserved.
    - Transparent click-through `main` window: not touched. No
      tauri.conf.json / lib.rs / setIgnoresMouseEvents_ changes.
    
    Docs:
    - docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md §4 native-DnD paragraph + cross-ref
      to SPIKE-FINDINGS.
    - docs/workflow/roadmap/codex-reviews/g3-organizer-batch/PROCESS-NOTE.md
      P0-Foxtrot resolution narrative.
    - grid-shell-organizer-content/docs/dev_log.md Work Log row.
    
